# Resilience (Resilience4j)

## Retry

- @Retry on method or Retry.of("name"); config: maxAttempts, waitDuration, retryExceptions; use for transient failures (5xx, connection).
- Do not retry 4xx (except 429 with backoff); use retryOnException predicate.

## Circuit Breaker

- @CircuitBreaker or CircuitBreaker.of("name"); config: failureRateThreshold, waitDurationInOpenState, slidingWindowSize.
- States: CLOSED → OPEN after threshold; OPEN → HALF_OPEN after wait; HALF_OPEN → CLOSED on success.
- Use for external HTTP/DB to fail fast when backend is down.

## Rate Limiter / Bulkhead

- RateLimiter: limit calls per period.
- Bulkhead: limit concurrent calls (semaphore or thread pool) to isolate failure.
- Use when calling rate-limited or fragile external APIs.

## RestClient Integration

- Use Resilience4j RestClient customization (Retry, CircuitBreaker) via ExchangeFilterFunction or dedicated builder; or wrap call in decorator.
- Apply per client or per operation; use same circuit name for same backend.

## Conventions

- Retry for transients; circuit breaker for external services; timeout on RestClient; log state changes; metric for monitoring.

## Anti-Patterns

- Retrying 4xx; no circuit breaker for flaky services; no timeout; unbounded concurrency

**See also:** `http-clients.mdc`, `error-handling.mdc`
